1	/**
2	 * cli.ts — Tiny helper for building `--flag value` argv arrays from a typed
3	 * options object.
4	 *
5	 * Used on the *workflow-authoring* side (src/workflows/*.wac.ts, which may
6	 * import types -- and this pure helper -- from this self-contained
7	 * directory) so that invoking a script from a workflow step is checked
8	 * against that script's own exported `Args` interface: a typo'd or missing
9	 * required flag is a compile error, not a silently-wrong `bun run` command
10	 * discovered only at workflow-run time.
11	 *
12	 * Scope of the guarantee: this checks flag *names* and *shape* (required vs
13	 * optional, string/number/boolean) at TypeScript-authoring time. It cannot
14	 * check the runtime *value* GitHub Actions substitutes in (e.g.
15	 * `${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}`), since that's a bash-level
16	 * expression resolved only when the workflow actually runs -- an inherent
17	 * limit of generating shell commands, not something any TS layer can close.
18	 */
19	/**
20	 * Read the flags a script knows, ignoring loudly any it does not.
21	 *
