15	 * ## Why it only looks at requests newer than the run
16	 *
17	 * A stop from last week is not a stop of this run. Without the cutoff, an issue that
18	 * was ever stopped could never be worked on again: every run would find the old
19	 * request on its first poll and stop before doing anything.
20	 *
21	 * ## Why it never fails the step
22	 *
23	 * It is a background process inside the step that runs the agent. Exiting non-zero
24	 * would say the run failed, and "GitHub returned a 502 while we were polling" is not
25	 * a failed run. A poll that cannot answer is treated as "no stop yet", which is the
26	 * answer that lets work continue.
